# REGRESSION — a String view into a collection the binding OWNS survives that
# collection growing past a reallocation.
#
# CELL: source shape = an OWNED collection (not a borrow, not an alias) ·
# the source reallocs on a forward path from the bind · element type String.
#
#     Vector[String] owned_copy = v       # eager clone at the bind, see below
#     String s = owned_copy.get(0).unwrap()
#     ... grow owned_copy 64x -> realloc ...
#     print(s)                            # must survive
#
# WHY THE BIND IS A COPY, MEASURED — this is NOT a sever, and no alias is
# ever created. A bare-identifier bind takes the CoW ALIAS branch
# (`src/ir/lowering/stmts/mod.rs:1498-1509`) only when neither the destination
# nor the SOURCE is reassigned on a forward path (`is_cow_unsafe_at`). Here `v`
# IS reassigned below, so the branch is skipped, the bind falls through to the
# eager-clone path, and `owned_copy` is an owned `Vector__GorgetString` from
# the start. Instrumenting the sole producer of `BorrowOrigin::Alias`
# (`cow_register_alias`) shows ZERO calls for this program; deleting the
# `v = []` line makes it fire. So the reassignment's PRESENCE PREVENTS the
# alias from forming -- it does not sever one.
#
# MECHANISM PIN + FIRE COUNT: the sibling harness assertion checks the emitted
# GIR carries the lazy rescue (`__cow_mat == 1`). stdout cannot distinguish
# "the rescue ran" from "nothing needed rescuing" -- this program prints
# `hello` either way. The count is RED (`found 0`) when the rescue is broken:
# force `source_mut_unsafe` to `false` at its computation in
# `src/ir/lowering/stmts/mod.rs` and rebuild. That break has been run.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT PIN: this cell does NOT exercise the collection-identity
# resolution it arrived with. Its fire count is `__cow_mat=1` on the pre-fix
# compiler too -- the provenance recorded is the same either way, because
# there is no alias chain to resolve. It pins the pre-existing lazy rescue on
# an OWNED source, a cell nothing else in the corpus covered.
#
# The lengths pin that `owned_copy` and `v` are independent values: the copy
# grew to 65 while `v` kept the single element it was given afterwards.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(mk("hel", "lo"))
    Vector[String] owned_copy = v
    v = []
    v.push(mk("new", "one"))
    String s = owned_copy.get(0).unwrap()
    int i = 0
    while i < 64:
        owned_copy.push(mk("fill", "er"))
        i = i + 1
    print(s)
    print(owned_copy.len())
    print(v.len())
